[General] Once this branch picks up #19366, `getServerAddress()` returns IPv6 addresses without brackets, so `jdbc:postgresql://[2001:db8::1]:5432/orders` derives the name `2001:db8::1:5432/orders`, which is an ambiguous host/port representation. `UrlParsingUtils.buildShortUrl` brackets IPv6 hosts for the same reason. This matches the handling requested in the sibling pool instrumentation PRs.

Could you also add a name-derivation test with an IPv6 URL, e.g. `jdbc:postgresql://[2001:db8::1]:5432/orders` -> `[2001:db8::1]:5432/orders`?

```suggestion
    if (serverAddress != null) {
      if (serverAddress.indexOf(':') >= 0 && !serverAddress.startsWith("[")) {
        poolName.append('[').append(serverAddress).append(']');
      } else {
        poolName.append(serverAddress);
      }
      if (serverPort != null) {
        poolName.append(':').append(serverPort);
      }
    }
```

